        "location": "place_solar_platform",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "6. Compare Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn",
          "description": "The heliocentric view returns with Earth, Mars, Jupiter (5.2 AU), and Saturn (9.5 AU). Step through a retrograde event for each and observe the loop sizes: Mars about 15 degrees, Jupiter about 10 degrees, Saturn about 7 degrees. More distant planets show smaller loops because Earth's orbital motion subtends a smaller angle from farther away, the same parallax geometry that makes nearby objects shift more than distant ones as you move your head. Click or say 'next' to review."
        },
